        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c929b35f6b5e431f9e357472f1e0139f",
      "statement": "The returned per-bone lists are unpacked with a loop bounded by the pose buffer's own bone count while indexing the Python arrays, so a Python side returning fewer bones than the rig reads past the end of those arrays and throws, which the stage catches — disabling itself and silently freezing the pose — while a Python side returning more bones has the surplus silently ignored.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionField/MotionFieldStage.cs#L296-L324",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8b26f0ae4fdde0ee42721e6321a165cd37b95e1c0f1d49bfd529abd63a69c98d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2a40f9e0d24e4286bd9527cb75cfd8c1",
      "statement": "The foot contacts the stage reports each frame come back from the policy call alongside the pose: each foot is down when the chosen action's neighbours, weighted as the action weighted their velocities, mostly have it down one frame later.",
      "evidence": [
